---
import DocHeading from "../../../replica/studio/DocHeading.astro";
import Prose from "../../../replica/studio/Prose.astro";
---

<Prose>
  <DocHeading level={1}>Implementation plan</DocHeading>
  <DocHeading level={2}>Approach</DocHeading>
  <p>
    Add one keyboard hook that the app shell mounts once. It opens the existing search dialog, so
    search itself does not change.
  </p>
  <DocHeading level={2}>Design</DocHeading>
  <DocHeading level={3}><code>src/search/use-search-shortcut.ts</code></DocHeading>
  <p>
    New hook. It listens for <code>keydown</code> on <code>window</code>, matches{" "}
    <code>metaKey</code> on macOS and <code>ctrlKey</code> elsewhere, and ignores{" "}
    <code>Shift</code>. It returns early for text fields, <code>[contenteditable]</code>, and open
    modal dialogs.
  </p>
  <DocHeading level={3}><code>src/app/app-shell.tsx</code></DocHeading>
  <p>Mounts the hook once and passes <code>openSearch</code>.</p>
  <DocHeading level={3}><code>src/search/search-dialog.tsx</code></DocHeading>
  <p>Stores the focused element when the dialog opens and restores it when it closes.</p>
  <DocHeading level={2}>Requirement coverage</DocHeading>
  <ul>
    <li>Open search: the hook calls <code>openSearch</code> unless a modal dialog is open.</li>
    <li>Text fields: the hook checks the event target.</li>
    <li>Close: the dialog restores focus.</li>
  </ul>
  <DocHeading level={2}>Tests</DocHeading>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>use-search-shortcut.test.ts</code>: the shortcut opens search, and does nothing with{
        " "
      }
      <code>Shift</code>, in a text field, or over a modal dialog.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <DocHeading level={2}>Risks and constraints</DocHeading>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>src/app/keymap.ts</code> binds <code>Cmd+Shift+K</code>, so the hook ignores{" "}
      <code>Shift</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Prose>
